  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_leto",
      "name": {
        "en": "Leto's Badge",
        "zh": "烈夏证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_leto",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Leto has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for wide-range enemy suppression.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Guard Operator during field operations to exercise Lord responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员烈夏擅长在较大范围内阻击敌人\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为近卫干员，行使领主职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_leto",
      "name": {
        "en": "The Old Clothes",
        "zh": "旧衣服",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "Y",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_leto",
      "description": {
        "en": "At first, not everyone got along particularly well.\nThat pretty much goes without saying.\nLada would silently hide behind Sonya. Anna wasn't any better; though she was clearly trying to keep her emotions in check, I could tell that she was panicking. Sonya felt like she had a duty to protect the others, so she kept her hand tightly gripped around her axe. I always thought her hand was going to slip one of these days.\nUnder that atmosphere, everyone was constantly on edge. And to make matters worse, nobody knew if what we were doing was right or wrong.\nLada wanted to be of help—she felt like she was always sheltered by Sonya, and was afraid of being left behind—so she'd go out and try to find us something to eat, though she came back with empty hands most of the times. Anna wanted the group to be more 'stable,' so she'd try to strike up conversations, but they seldom went the way she wanted. Sonya was generally in high spirits, but every so often she'd come back with an extra wound or two.\nEveryone did their best to get something done, as if they'd go mad if they didn't. Though sometimes, you could get rid of the 'as if' part.\nAs for me, I was never that scared in the first place, but it's not like I'd have been happy dying there. I didn't want to lose Sonya and the others either—we'd been friends already. So, I also did whatever I could: bringing back supplies, helping Sonya 'take out the trash,' and even teaching some harsh lessons to anyone who tried to lay their hands on Anna.\nAt first I thought things would get better, but it was actually the opposite. Lada and Anna started avoiding eye contact with me, and even Sonya would strangely glare at me. That's when I understood: I'd been robbing them of their agency.\nBut I was better at those things, so why shouldn't I do it?\nOf course, I was never the petty type, and it's not like Lada or Sonya really blamed me for that. I knew they were both real nice, we just didn't know how to get along back then. It wasn't until the day Sonya came back from a scuffle with a serious tear in her uniform and Anna used a sewing kit I'd scavenged to fix it up that I realized what I needed to do.\nI snuck into the warehouse, found some coats, and brought them to Anna to ask her if she could fix them up into something more cold-resistant. We'd need them later when the weather turned cold, and sure enough, she cheered up at that.\nAfter that, I risked my hide to steal some Reunion kitchenware for Lada so it'd be easier for her to cook, though obviously it was better to keep that part low-key. Her eyes lit up the instant she saw what I brought back.\nI even found some self-defense equipment for everyone, and modified them with Sonya. While we were working together, I thumped my chest and said to her: If there's anything you want, just say the word and I'll get it for you. Sonya stared at me for a while, but this time, she nodded.\nLooking back now, it was probably around then that our team actually started taking shape.",
        "zh": "大家一开始相处得并不好。\n这也是理所当然的事情。\n拉达起初经常躲在索尼娅的背后一句话也不说。安娜的状况也好不到哪里去，她虽然在极力克制自己的情绪，但我看得出来，她也很慌张。索尼娅觉得她有责任保护其他人，整天都把她那把斧子握得很紧，我猜，总有一天她会不小心松手的。\n这样的氛围下，大家都很敏感，更糟糕的是，大家都不知道自己在做的事情对不对，好不好。\n拉达想要让自己变得有用——她觉得自己总是受到索尼娅的庇护，害怕哪天就被抛下——她想要去找一些食物回来，但总是碰壁。安娜想要让这个团体变得更“安定”，经常找各种人对话，可对话的结果往往不如她所愿。索尼娅虽然还挺精神，但她的身上隔一段时间就会多一道伤口。\n大家都在拼命让自己做些事情，仿佛不这么做就会疯掉——好吧，也许可以去掉“仿佛”两个字。\n至于我，虽然我一开始就不怎么害怕，但要是真的死在这里，那我是不乐意的。我也不希望失去索尼娅她们，我们已经是朋友了。所以，我也去做了许多我能做的事——带回一些物资，帮索尼娅收拾几个人，还悄悄教训了那些想要对安娜动手的家伙。\n我原本以为这样会变得好一点，结果反而变得糟糕了，拉达和安娜看我的眼神变得有些躲闪，索尼娅有时也会盯着我看。这时，我明白了，我抢了她们想做的事。\n但是，这些事原本就是我更加擅长，为什么不能由我来做呢？\n当然，我也没有这么小心眼，就好像拉达和安娜也没有因此对我做什么——我知道她们都很好，只是我们那时候还不知道如何相处。直到有一天，索尼娅因为和人发生冲突，校服上被狠狠地划了一道口子，安娜用我找来的针线包帮她把衣服缝好，我才忽然明白了我该做什么。\n我偷偷溜进仓库，找来一些大衣，交给安娜，希望她能帮我们改造成更加耐寒的衣服，天气变得更冷了，接下来用得着。果然，安娜一听，就高兴了起来。\n接着，我又冒险去偷了些整合运动的厨具给拉达，让她能更好地做菜，当然，最好是偷偷地做。拉达也一下子高兴了起来。\n我还给大家找来了一些防身的玩意，和索尼娅一边讨论，一边改造。我拍着胸脯和索尼娅说，想要什么就告诉我，我去帮大家弄。索尼娅盯了我一会儿，这回，她点了点头。\n现在想起来，大概是从那时候起，我们的团队才真正有了一个雏形吧。",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
